Exp :Reverse Number

Aim:
To write a Java program to reverse a given number.

Algorithm:
1. Start the program.
2. Import the Scanner package.
3. Read a number from the user.
4. Initialize reverse = 0.
5. Extract the last digit using n % 10.
6. Add the digit to the reverse number using reverse = reverse * 10 + digit.
7. Remove the last digit using n = n / 10.
8. Repeat until the number becomes zero.
9. Display the reversed number.
10. Stop the program.

Program:

import java.util.Scanner;
public class ReverseNumber {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        int n, digit, reverse = 0;

        System.out.print("Enter a number: ");
        n = sc.nextInt();

        while (n != 0) {
            digit = n % 10;
            reverse = reverse * 10 + digit;
            n = n / 10;
        }

        System.out.println("Reverse number = " + reverse);

        sc.close();
    }
}

Output:
Enter a number: 1234
Reverse number = 4321

Result:
Thus, the Java program to reverse a given number was executed successfully.
